  <section id="safety-gear">
    <h2>Packing Your Essential Kayak Safety Gear</h2>
    <p>
      Essential River Kayaking Safety for Beginners
    </p>
    <p>
      Mastering river kayaking safety for beginners is the foundation of every successful paddling trip. Moving water behaves very differently from a calm lake or the sea. Without the right knowledge and equipment, a fun day out can quickly turn into a dangerous rescue situation.
    </p>
    <p>
      Before you load up your boat, you must understand how to read the water, equip yourself properly, and know your limits.
    </p>
    <p>
      You should never get in a boat without the right equipment. The most critical piece of essential kayak safety gear is a properly fitted Personal Flotation Device (PFD) or buoyancy aid. Unlike a life jacket, a PFD allows for the full range of motion needed to paddle.
    </p>
    <p>Additionally, always carry:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>A Throwline:</strong> Essential for rescuing a fellow paddler from the bank.</li>
      <li><strong>A Whistle:</strong> Attached securely to your PFD to signal for help.</li>
      <li><strong>A Communication Device:</strong> A fully charged mobile phone in a high-quality waterproof pouch.</li>
    </ul>
